project/editor-crossscreen-polish: spoint editor cross-screen engine-editor patterns (kit anentrypoint-design 0.0.183+, consumed via unpkg @latest). (1) APPS list = flat .ds-ep-tree rows (twist+label+tag+inline ghost-dense Place btn) + inline file expand, container ds-ep-panel; NOT C.Panel/C.Row cards (those render giant double-nested cards w/ pills). (2) INSPECTOR transform = vecField as a .ds-ep-propfield.block (label above) with .ds-ep-vec3 (flex, 3 equal-width fields) so x/y/z pack on ONE row not stacked boxes; Body Type also .block so the 3-segment IconButtonGroup spans full width and does not clip the narrow value column; Edit/Delete in a flush .ds-ep-actionbar (dense buttons, not pills). (3) MOBILE (max-width:760px): the 3D viewport MUST stay visible. Mark the viewport placeholder .ep-viewport-pane and in the editor responsive CSS pull its split-pane order:-1 flex:0 0 40vh overflow:hidden to the top; cap side+inspector :not(:has(.ep-viewport-pane)) at ~48vh scroll. Without this the stacked panels fully occlude the canvas. Witness with elementFromPoint(cx,y) returning CANVAS in the top band. (4) FLUSH edges: kit .app-main carries a dashboard gutter; override .ep-overlay .app-main{padding:0} so panels dock to screen edges (sceneX 32->0). (5) Events tab = flat .ds-ep-eventrow console rows not C.EventList cards; HookFlow off C.Panel onto ds-ep-panel. Kit buttons stay pill-shaped unless dense+CSS: .ds-ep-tree-row/.ds-ep-toolbar/.ds-ep-actionbar buttons are height-constrained in editor-primitives.css. Witnessed phone/tablet/desktop/ultrawide, no hoverflow any width.